Review proposals: note writes that wait for your decision.

A session in the `propose` mode, such as a reflection pass, does not write a note. It makes a proposal. The file on disk changes only when you accept the proposal.

Examples:
  # The proposals that wait for you
  cru proposal list

  # The diff of one proposal
  cru proposal show <id>

  # Write it, or refuse it with a reason
  cru proposal accept <id>
  cru proposal reject <id> --reason "the note says the opposite"

  # Take a superseded proposal out of the Inbox
  cru proposal dismiss <id>

Usage: proposal <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list     List the proposals in the Inbox
  show     Show a proposal and the diff of each file
  accept   Write every file of a proposal
  reject   Reject a proposal. The files do not change
  dismiss  Take a proposal out of the Inbox with no decision
  resolve  Give the settled text of one conflicted file
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
